<title>ITALY: Italy hopes EU okays Alitalia plan soon.</title>
<headline>Italy hopes EU okays Alitalia plan soon.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian transport minister Claudio Burlando said he hoped the European Commission would give its go-ahead for a rescue plan for troubled state airline Alitalia before the end of the year.</p>
<p>&quot;The first thing is to get the European Union's consensus and I hope that this will come by autumn,&quot; Burlando told reporters after a cabinet meeting.</p>
<p>&quot;Once this is resolved, in a positive way I hope, we can get started with what the plan envisages, that is to say that which the EU will have approved,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Industrial state industrial holding company IRI, Alitalia's majority sharerholder, approved at the beginning of July a 1.5 trillion lire capital increase for the struggling carrier.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
